diff --git a/docs/operations/clamav-repair.md b/docs/operations/clamav-repair.md
index dfac70e3..187006fb 100644
--- a/docs/operations/clamav-repair.md
+++ b/docs/operations/clamav-repair.md
@@ -1,5 +1,17 @@
 # Protected ClamAV repair
 
+## Explicit degraded-instance incident recovery
+
+Ordinary repair still requires a healthy, rehearsed previous scanner and is unchanged. An already degraded installation cannot truthfully supply that proof. `DEPLOYMENT_CLAMAV_OPERATION=incident-recovery` is a separate incident operation on the exact deployed source base; it is not an ordinary application release and cannot contain business changes or migrations. The source-scope gate and every checkpoint, lease, mutation deadline, complete-release gate and post-open rollback prohibition still apply.
+
+Before entering maintenance, prepare and review a real healthy target with current publisher signatures, successful FreshClam cycle, matching loaded bank, CLEAN and streamed EICAR rejection. Record the actual running original with `node scripts/clamav-incident-recovery.mjs snapshot <container> <private-file>`, then supply that file as `DEPLOYMENT_CLAMAV_INCIDENT_SNAPSHOT_FILE`. Do not supply a rollback-health proof in incident mode. The read-only snapshot records its image, effective configuration hash, exact signed bank hashes/versions and specific observed degradation. It explicitly denies reopening the original. Preflight re-inspects the original; the durable owned session binds the operation and snapshot checksum. Capture rechecks those bytes and the stopped original before the full encrypted checkpoint is independently read back.
+
+Only after the complete local and independent checkpoint passes may the journal enter mutation and activate the authenticated target image/bank. All six release identities form the resulting complete release set; rebuilding maintenance-only application images does not authorize business-source changes. On any failure after maintenance begins, never reopen the known-degraded original as a successful rollback. After mutation, the one coordinated restore recovers its exact data, original bank/configuration, numeric ownership and cooldown, then retains maintenance in `RECOVERY_REQUIRED`. The restored scanner remains stopped rather than making an uncontrolled update attempt. An unresolved incident blocks subsequent ordinary releases. Failure before maintenance leaves the running original untouched. This availability trade-off preserves ADR-0039's fail-closed recovery rule; it supplies no health exception.
+
+For acquisition, Cisco's supported `cvdupdate` may prepare a publisher-signed bank on another authorized network; retain its version, official origin, checksums and signature-verification evidence. That evidence is not updater-health evidence. Recurring production acquisition remains FreshClam with `TestDatabases yes`, normal persistent scheduling and unchanged signature verification. The fixed HTTPS FEUP mirror (`https://mirrors.fe.up.pt/pub/clamav`) serves official signed CVD/CDIFF files; official `current.cvd.clamav.net` DNS remains the independent freshness authority. No arbitrary mirror, custom database URL, TLS bypass or fallback request to a CDN currently refusing requests is introduced. Preserve existing cooldown and scheduler files; importing a signed file alone cannot manufacture a successful cycle or advance its next eligible update slot. Verify the chosen mirror using a real naturally eligible FreshClam cycle before activation, and a later natural cycle before incident closure. See [ClamAV's mirror guidance](https://docs.clamav.net/appendix/CvdPrivateMirror.html) and the [FEUP mirror index](https://mirrors.fe.up.pt/pub/clamav/).
+
+An explicitly authorized acquisition-source migration may be prepared with `node scripts/clamav-source-migration.mjs prepare <inactive-CDN-bank> <verified-CVD-directory> <new-inactive-bank>`. This creates a new destination exclusively: it never edits the refusing origin or resets an existing mirror identity. Exact vendor `freshclam.dat`, scheduler and result-log bytes remain under `.source-state/vendor-cdn`, with their hashes, original numeric metadata and declared deadline bound into `.source-state/migration.json`. FreshClam itself does not provide per-origin cooldown identities; this is a reviewed migration to a different fixed acquisition service. The independent mirror identity begins unhealthy, with no copied success state, and cannot attempt acquisition before the last real attempt plus the normal 7,200-second interval. All of this state is carried in the authenticated bank/checkpoint. No vendor-CDN fallback exists; any future return requires a separately reviewed operation honoring its retained refusal. Recreate never reruns preparation over an existing bank. Readiness verifies both the effective acquisition configuration and archived vendor hashes in addition to the real mirror update and scanner gates. Keep archived provenance readable but not writable by the updater.
+
 This is a maintenance-only repair, independent of attendance R3. No schema, attendance, correction, PDF or shared-duty behavior is changed. Cloud execution, deployment and automatic attendance require separate authorization. Local test success does not prove cloud readiness.
 
 ## Local runtime
